.$ Finally, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =2+6i \\\\  & =6\\,i+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79c85169-b2cd-5195-a225-395f470200b5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Complex Number With No Real or No Imaginary Part Represented by an Argand Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81d61478-cb99-59d7-b8e3-440f768af1eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058862} {:answer/id #uuid "a0c74234-883d-55b7-91b1-880b3ed7e934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 2\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058863} {:answer/id #uuid "c837d15c-a188-5101-a986-21318e57ceff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z =-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058864} {:answer/id #uuid "1a89f244-fb14-5391-91e3-ee6e8f5309ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z =-2\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058865} {:answer/id #uuid "629b1547-2da4-507f-ac7d-03ad9e5af44b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a89f244-fb14-5391-91e3-ee6e8f5309ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z =-2\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058865} :answer-field/id #uuid "5582e440-b87c-53e1-9393-8bdfe610da74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058861}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aba305a7-4fcc-5a97-9e41-40a6cfb6c6b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-69768" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/assets/51c45ca80f9b3f0593c6d2aef8dc55ca836a208db1d10b7e6ba5f77cb43f029d.png)\n\nWhat complex number is represented in the Argand diagram above?" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the point are $(0,-2).$\n\n- The real part of this complex number is $x=0,$ and\n\n- the imaginary part is $y=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the number depicted is $z=0-2\\text{i},$ which can be simplfied to $z=-2\\text{i}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297164 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4b612ef-ce7f-5783-848d-d8ef210c9f47" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Argand Diagram Corresponding to a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "166682f6-ab26-5f5f-812f-14c3bc9a0882" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297166} {:answer/id #uuid "df4c7f88-aafe-50bc-9d63-942e9f9951f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297167} {:answer/id #uuid "ede556e2-fb3a-5636-856f-d24dd4da63da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297168} {:answer/id #uuid "66064b9a-caec-5ba3-809b-0368cce45795" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297169} {:answer/id #uuid "9830ee31-d229-5e50-a59b-c72a74309405" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df4c7f88-aafe-50bc-9d63-942e9f9951f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297167} :answer-field/id #uuid "0be00c72-62e9-5718-858c-6102d0b60075" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297165}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5f599a30-a12e-5fb2-b8d4-552e44102ddc" :question/math-academy-id "q-69899" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers lie in the second quadrant in an Argand diagram?\n\n- $-2+\\text{i}$\n- $-3-2\\text{i}$\n- $-3+2\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "- The complex number $-2+\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-2$ and the imaginary part $y=1.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-2,1)$, which lies in the second quadrant.\n\n- The complex number $-3-2\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-3$ and the imaginary part $y=-2.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-3,-2)$, which lies in the third quadrant.\n\n- The complex number $-3+2\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-3$ and the imaginary part $y=2.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-3,2)$, which lies in the second quadrant.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/assets/d683b808bee4b7893952adbaf87940066f9ff7d61c99ce7cc7e05fc9a4fbe02f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297171 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4b612ef-ce7f-5783-848d-d8ef210c9f47" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Argand Diagram Corresponding to a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e8859b7-0f64-5ffd-b7c2-4e0e67dee555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297173} {:answer/id #uuid "3c28c7f9-8ca1-5cf2-9890-3d34ef9c1360" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297174} {:answer/id #uuid "1a372308-09e2-5f67-8854-d0eb6851abb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297175} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d6efa8-0ff9-5436-ae42-892b7a58160d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297176} {:answer/id #uuid "53372f5e-6f6d-5f76-8c1c-990c2a0e2fde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e8859b7-0f64-5ffd-b7c2-4e0e67dee555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297173} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d6f6b19-e2fe-5b08-9b09-412380ff9a59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f8058154-02f7-5ef9-8152-a44cf9d8a038" :question/math-academy-id "q-79457" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers lie in the second quadrant in the corresponding Argand diagram?\n\n- $-2-2\\text{i}$\n- $-2+\\text{i}$\n- $-1+2\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "- The complex number $-2-2\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-2$ and the imaginary part $y=-2.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-2,-2)$, which lies in the third quadrant.\n\n- The complex number $-2+\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-2$ and the imaginary part $y=1.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-2,1)$, which lies in the second quadrant.\n\n- The complex number $-1+2\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-1$ and the imaginary part $y=2.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-1,2)$, which lies in the second quadrant.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/assets/9f2e7234ba52d14098e0ecfc9695181b425764c110995b76b4b0efddf206252c.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297178 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4b612ef-ce7f-5783-848d-d8ef210c9f47" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Argand Diagram Corresponding to a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3e92eae-9728-55ba-bb10-31efa5cc23fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297180} {:answer/id #uuid "3beb8cef-4fe7-5d0f-ad24-43527c1021b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297181} {:answer/id #uuid "c1f6ef17-a02d-5d57-961a-c54ff482baa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297182} {:answer/id #uuid "796ba084-620d-5601-bff3-60f2258c3d4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297183} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a8b3b9-b92f-5d1f-96e6-db3a14c320c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1f6ef17-a02d-5d57-961a-c54ff482baa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297182} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4fb5069-0f28-5454-ad98-782d2f4bac5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "15b01c05-a846-58d7-9fe9-046ca9485817" :question/math-academy-id "q-79458" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers lie in the fourth quadrant in an Argand diagram?\n\n- $\\frac{3}{2}-\\text{i}$\n- $-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{i}$\n- $\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "- The complex number $\\frac{3}{2}-\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=\\frac{3}{2}$ and the imaginary part $y=-1.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(\\frac{3}{2},-1)$, which lies in the fourth quadrant.\n\n- The complex number $-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and the imaginary part $y=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{2})$, which lies in the third quadrant.\n\n- The complex number $\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ and the imaginary part $y=\\frac{3}{2}.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2})$, which lies in the first quadrant.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/assets/d7390ddcc8d338d2fd46bc12b0a4c65f8e6bf6e8c4f6c9fa802e2acea159416b.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297185 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "79c85169-b2cd-5195-a225-395f470200b5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Complex Number With No Real or No Imaginary Part Represented by an Argand Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a2fb103-c110-57eb-9a75-681b0be86989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=1-4\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297187} {:answer/id #uuid "e9b4e153-c077-574a-aedf-bcc8dce90b4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=-4+\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297188} {:answer/id #uuid "1e4cb32e-bbeb-514b-b3c1-35a9e89ebb39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=4\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297189} {:answer/id #uuid "c20df022-7bdc-5ccb-9171-ad3e2a86854d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=-4\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297190} {:answer/id #uuid "46234f01-7804-5979-bfaf-04c6ca506f8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e4cb32e-bbeb-514b-b3c1-35a9e89ebb39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=4\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297189} :answer-field/id #uuid "57ed1a73-1dfc-50f8-a867-17a0e033a043" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297186}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c837b5e3-6f8e-55dd-9399-088986a8120d" :question/math-academy-id "q-8244" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/assets/da9c358095b4c01d409998bbdcb98b7260f508463a44723c9b00e48ec1f61424.png)\n\nWhat complex number is represented in the Argand diagram above?" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the point are $(0,4).$\n\n- The real part of this complex number is $x=0,$ and\n\n- the imaginary part is $y=4.$\n\nTherefore, the number depicted is $z=0+4\\text{i},$ which can be simplified to $z=4\\text{i}.$"}]}
